From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 09:49:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] netd.c: let the 4.9 stats programs load on any API level

The ingress/egress stats program table covers kernel 4.9 with one
variant, stats$4_9_t, whose loader range stops at V. On a 4.9 kernel
running 25Q2+ nothing is pinned at netd_shared/prog_netd_{ingress,egress}_stats,
and netd's BpfHandler::init aborts on ENOENT when it attaches them.
Every other variant starts at 4.19, so widening $4_9_t to MAXAPI
overlaps nothing.
---
 bpf/progs/netd.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bpf/progs/netd.c b/bpf/progs/netd.c
index e4cd7c93b4..223640c19b 100644
--- a/bpf/progs/netd.c
+++ b/bpf/progs/netd.c
@@ -1025,8 +1025,8 @@ DEFINE_NETD_BPF_PROG_RANGES(ingress, stats, 4_19, 5_4, T, 25Q2)
 return bpf_traffic_account(skb, INGRESS, KVER_4_19, API(T));
 }
 
-// Android T 4.9 & T/U 4.14
-DEFINE_NETD_BPF_PROG_RANGES(ingress, stats, 4_9, 4_19, T, V)
+// Android T 4.9 & T/U 4.14 (and the only variant a 4.9 kernel can load on anything newer)
+DEFINE_NETD_BPF_PROG_RANGES(ingress, stats, 4_9, 4_19, T, MAXAPI)
 (struct __sk_buff* skb) {
     return bpf_traffic_account(skb, INGRESS, KVER_4_9, API(T));
 }
@@ -1081,8 +1081,8 @@ DEFINE_NETD_BPF_PROG_RANGES(egress, stats, 4_19, 5_4, T, 25Q2)
 return bpf_traffic_account(skb, EGRESS, KVER_4_19, API(T));
 }
 
-// Android T 4.9 & T/U 4.14
-DEFINE_NETD_BPF_PROG_RANGES(egress, stats, 4_9, 4_19, T, V)
+// Android T 4.9 & T/U 4.14 (and the only variant a 4.9 kernel can load on anything newer)
+DEFINE_NETD_BPF_PROG_RANGES(egress, stats, 4_9, 4_19, T, MAXAPI)
 (struct __sk_buff* skb) {
     return bpf_traffic_account(skb, EGRESS, KVER_4_9, API(T));
 }
